Job Description

The Sales Trainee role offers hands-on exposure to FMCG sales operations and market execution. The position focuses on managing distribution, improving market reach, driving business growth, and ensuring effective execution of sales strategies across assigned territories.

Key Responsibilities

Achieve territory sales targets and business objectives.
Execute distribution and outlet coverage plans to maximize market reach and product availability.
Implement trade schemes, consumer promotions, and merchandising initiatives.
Manage distributor operations and ensure efficient stock planning and availability.
Monitor sales performance, analyze data, and recommend corrective actions.
Build strong relationships with retailers, distributors, and trade partners.
Track competitive activities and provide market intelligence.
Ensure adherence to company policies, statutory requirements, and operational processes.
Skills & Competencies

Sales Planning & Execution
Territory Management
Distributor & Channel Management
Business Analytics & Reporting
Customer Relationship Management
Negotiation & Influencing Skills
Problem Solving & Market Development
Eligibility Criteria

Students must meet the following criteria to apply:

MBA / PGDM with Marketing Specialization.
2027 Pass Out Batch only.
Minimum 50% marks throughout academic career.
No academic year loss due to backlogs.
Must be a permanent resident of the designated hiring location/state.
Proficiency in the local language (Read, Write, and Speak).
Willingness to travel extensively (up to 25 days per month).
Age should not exceed 25 years.
Selection Process

The recruitment process will consist of:

Aptitude Test
Group Discussion (GD)
Technical/Functional Interview
HR/Managerial Interview
Candidates who successfully clear each stage will progress to the subsequent round.

Career Progression

ITC offers a structured and performance-driven career path:

Sales Trainee (STR) → Sales Officer → Area Executive → Area Manager

Join as a Sales Trainee with a starting CTC of ₹4.5 LPA.
High-performing trainees are typically considered for progression to Sales Officer within 12 months.
Subsequent growth opportunities include Area Executive and Area Manager roles with increased responsibilities and leadership opportunities.
Why Join ITC Sales?

Early ownership and responsibility for business outcomes.
Exposure to multiple FMCG categories and sales channels.
Structured learning, coaching, and career development programs.
Opportunity to work on leading brands and build commercial expertise.
Clearly defined and accelerated career growth path.
Strong platform to develop leadership and business management capabilities.
